Id: cron008w
Severity: WARN
Category: cron
Check: check_crontabs
Fix: chmod g-w the file.
References: crontab(5), cron(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A file cron reads (/etc/crontab, a file in /etc/cron.d, a script in
/etc/cron.hourly, cron.daily, cron.weekly or cron.monthly, or a user's
crontab in the spool) can be written by its group. Every member of the
group decides what cron runs from it, and as whom: root, for every file
but a user's own crontab. Debian's spool crontabs belong to the group
crontab without its being able to write them; that is not this.

Take the group's write permission away (chmod g-w), unless every member
of the group is meant to have root.
